# Fibonacci Shader Grid — a Skia runtime shader (XorDev-style phyllotaxis of
# glowing dots) masked by a blurred circle and animated by a 20 s ping-pong
# clock; a 2D pad below drives two uniforms: X = number of circles (5..175),
# Y = the angle multiplier (1.2..3.6).
# What this test covers: taps at the pad's four corners and centre (spring
# with overshoot on both uniforms, incl. N briefly below its minimum), slow
# drags along each axis, a drag that leaves the pad on every side (clamped
# remap), a fast diagonal sweep, interrupting a spring with a new touch, and
# letting the shader animate between steps. Pad: x 110..296, y 520..706.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/fibonacci-shader-grid"
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 30000
wait 2000
# Corners: (min N, min mul), (max, min), (max, max), (min, max), centre.
press 114 524
wait 1000
press 292 524
wait 1000
press 292 702
wait 1000
press 114 702
wait 1000
press 203 613
wait 1000
# Slow drags along each axis.
gesture pan 115 613 175 0 1500
wait 600
gesture pan 203 525 0 175 1500
wait 600
# Out of the pad on every side (values must clamp).
gesture pan 203 613 -190 0 700
wait 500
gesture pan 203 613 190 0 700
wait 500
gesture pan 203 613 0 -150 700
wait 500
gesture pan 203 613 0 180 700
wait 500
# Fast diagonal sweep.
gesture pan 115 525 175 175 150
wait 800
# Interrupt a spring with a new touch.
press 114 524
wait 120
press 292 702
wait 120
press 203 613
wait 1500
# Let the shader run.
wait 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
